   "source": {
    "label": "thm:expected-regret-total",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For any $K$-arm bandit problem with reward distribution supported on $[0,1]$, KL-MS has regret bounded as follows. For any $\\Delta \\geq 0$ and $c \\in (0, \\frac14]$: \\Reg(T) \\leq T\\Delta + \\sum_{a: \\Delta_a > \\Delta} \\frac{\\Delta_a \\ln(T \\kl(\\mu_a + c \\Delta_a, \\mu_1 - c \\Delta_a) \\vee e^2 )}{\\kl(\\mu_a + c \\Delta_a, \\mu_1 - c \\Delta_a)} + 392 \\sum_{a: \\Delta_a > \\Delta} ..."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "dot mu_1 = mu_star(1-mu_star). Sums restricted to arms with gap > Delta_thr (sum_subopt used with that restriction). The appendix proof fixes c=1/4 for the constant 392 while the statement allows any c; recorded as stated."
